(

A6

). To a solution of intermediate 23 (100 mg, 0.29 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) were added CDI (51.9 mg, 0.32 mmol) and DIPEA (112.2 mg, 0.87 mmol). The resulting solution was stirred at room temperature for 1 h. Then, commercially available starting material 34 (128.2 mg, 0.35 mmol) was added to the above reaction system. The resulting solution was stirred at room temperature for 4 h. The reaction was monitored by TLC. Upon completion, the mixture was quenched with cool water (50 mL) at room temperature and extracted with EtOAc (50 mL × 3). The combined organic layers were washed with water, brine, and dried over Na2SO4. The drying agent was filtered off. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified via flash column chromatography (CH2Cl2/MeOH 47:3, v/v) to give compound A6 as a white solid, yield of 56%. m.p. 250.6–254.7 °C. Purity: 97.07% by analytical HPLC. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO‐d

6
