To a solution of intermediate 28 (50 mg, 0.15 mmol) in DMF (3 mL) were added 29 (59.65 mg, 0.20 mmol), DIPEA (59.60 mg, 0.46 mmol), HOBT (27.02 mg, 0.20 mmol), and EDCI (76.68 mg, 0.40 mmol). The resulting solution was stirred at room temperature for 3 h. The reaction was monitored by TLC. Upon completion, the mixture was quenched with cool water (30 mL) at room temperature and extracted with EtOAc (30 mL × 3). The combined organic layers were washed with water and brine and dried over Na2SO4. The drying agent was filtered off. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified via flash column chromatography (CH2Cl2/MeOH 19:1, v/v) to give compound B1 as a white solid, yield 74%. (R)‐2‐fluoro‐N‐((6‐(3‐methylmorpholino)‐2‐(1H‐pyrrolo[2,3‐b]pyridin‐4‐yl)pyrimidin‐4‐yl)methyl)‐5‐((4‐oxo‐3,4‐dihydrophthalazin‐1‐yl)methyl)benzamide (

B1
